; The declaration-phase DEPTH budget, which has existed since phase D
; did and was pinned by nothing: before this file the only occurrence
; of "declaration-macro expansion exceeded" anywhere in the tree was
; the line in `expand.ax` that emits it.
;
; `loopD` regenerates exactly one invocation of itself, so it never
; grows - it just never stops. `expDeclMacroRounds` stops it at 128
; rounds with AX3019, the same code the expression side raises for the
; same shape, and the message names rounds rather than forms because
; that is the axis phase D counts.
;
; It sits beside `401-decl-macro-size-limit`, and the pair is the
; point: one macro that recurses without growing and one that grows
; without recursing deeply, so a budget covering only one axis leaves
; a red gate behind rather than a silent hole.
(macro loopD ((loopD nm) (loopD nm)))

(loopD z)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
